Satori's patch to the pinned llama.cpp (b9574), applied by lib-llama-android/src/main/cpp/CMakeLists.txt
after 0002.

A load with mmap copies the weights it repacks (CPU_KLEIDIAI, CPU_REPACK) out of the GGUF's mapping,
and the mapping then holds those pages, mapped and cached, for as long as the model is loaded: 707 MB of
Gemma 3 1B's 1,019 MB, 999 MB of Gemma 4 E2B's 3,194 MB. This hands each mapping, with the byte ranges
of the tensors copied and of those used in place, to a hook ai_chat.cpp sets, once the last tensor is
loaded and before the loader unmaps the head and tail it doesn't use, so all of the mapping is still
mapped and the file still open. ai_chat.cpp gives the copied tensors' whole pages back there
(MADV_PAGEOUT, then MADV_DONTNEED). No hook is called until ai_chat.cpp sets one, so llama.cpp behaves
as it does without the patch. No line of it is within 3 lines of a hunk of 0001 or 0002, so each of the
three still passes git apply --reverse --check once all are in, as the CMake loop needs.

